{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.MassGapFrontier","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MassGapFrontier","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.MassGapObstruction","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.CrossingGradedModel"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.universality_transfers_obstruction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.universality_transfers_obstruction","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MassGapFrontier.lean#L183-L193","doc":"**What one `YMUniversality` instance would buy**: the Kummer\npersistence at all primes > 3 transfers from the QOU framework to\n*every* axiomatized gapped YM theory.  Proved sorry-free against\nthe interface; its physical force is exactly conditional on the\n(open) universality instance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YMUniversality.chi_is_minus_six","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YMUniversality.chi_is_minus_six","kind":"theorem","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MassGapFrontier.lean#L181-L181","doc":"The image context carries the QOU Euler characteristic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YMUniversality.toContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YMUniversality.toContext","kind":"def","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MassGapFrontier.lean#L179-L179","doc":"The structure map: axiomatized gapped YM ⟶ obstruction context. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YMUniversality.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YMUniversality.mk","kind":"ctor","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MassGapFrontier.lean#L177-L177","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YMUniversality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YMUniversality","kind":"class","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MassGapFrontier.lean#L165-L181","doc":"**The universality gate** (the Millennium-relevance interface):\na map sending every axiomatized gapped YM theory to a QOU\nobstruction-reduction context with `χ(A) = −6`.\n\n**No instance is provided or claimed** — constructing one (\"any\naxiomatized YM with a gap yields a QOU-type structure\") is the\nopen research identified by the workplan, and per its mandatory\ncaveat every obstruction statement remains QOU-framework-\nconditional until an instance exists.  This class pins the exact\nfield signature such a construction must satisfy. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AxiomatizedYMWithGap.gap_bounds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AxiomatizedYMWithGap.gap_bounds","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MassGapFrontier.lean#L163-L163","doc":"Every non-vacuum excitation energy is bounded below by the gap. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AxiomatizedYMWithGap.gap_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AxiomatizedYMWithGap.gap_pos","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MassGapFrontier.lean#L161-L161","doc":"The gap is strictly positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AxiomatizedYMWithGap.gap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AxiomatizedYMWithGap.gap","kind":"def","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MassGapFrontier.lean#L159-L159","doc":"The mass gap. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AxiomatizedYMWithGap.spectrum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AxiomatizedYMWithGap.spectrum","kind":"def","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MassGapFrontier.lean#L157-L157","doc":"The excitation spectrum (energies of states). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AxiomatizedYMWithGap.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AxiomatizedYMWithGap.mk","kind":"ctor","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MassGapFrontier.lean#L155-L155","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AxiomatizedYMWithGap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AxiomatizedYMWithGap","kind":"structure","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MassGapFrontier.lean#L150-L163","doc":"**Minimal abstract axiomatized YM-with-gap data**: an excitation\nspectrum and a uniform positive gap.  Deliberately free of any\nQOU-specific structure — these are the only fields the transfer\ncorollary consumes, so the universality gate is stated against\nthe weakest meaningful interface. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.crossingFiltration_of_base_and_transport","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.crossingFiltration_of_base_and_transport","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MassGapFrontier.lean#L132-L146","doc":"**Induction decomposition of the S1c hypothesis**: base case +\ntower transport ⟹ the full crossing-energy filtration.  The\nuniversally-quantified physical hypothesis is replaced by two\nstrictly smaller named hypotheses, matching the shape of the\nworkplan's preferred strategy (i). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TowerTransport.transport","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TowerTransport.transport","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MassGapFrontier.lean#L126-L126","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TowerTransport.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TowerTransport.mk","kind":"ctor","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MassGapFrontier.lean#L125-L125","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TowerTransport","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TowerTransport","kind":"class","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MassGapFrontier.lean#L117-L130","doc":"**Tower transport** (strategy (i), Wenzl/Jones-tower positivity):\nthe inclusion `H_n ⊂ H_{n+1}` with conditional expectation\npreserves the per-crossing bound — if every non-vacuum excitation\nat level `n` dominates `E_×(q)`, the same holds at level `n + 1`.\n\nThis is where the research content of S1c now lives: the\nconditional-expectation positivity argument supplies this field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.FiltrationBase.base","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.FiltrationBase.base","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MassGapFrontier.lean#L114-L114","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.FiltrationBase.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.FiltrationBase.mk","kind":"ctor","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MassGapFrontier.lean#L113-L113","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.FiltrationBase","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.FiltrationBase","kind":"class","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MassGapFrontier.lean#L109-L115","doc":"**Filtration base case**: the per-crossing bound holds at the\nbase level of the tower.  For the physical tower this is a fixed\nfinite-rank spectral computation (H₂ or H₃) — the\ncompute-witness + `native_decide` candidate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.crossing_eigenvalue_separation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.crossing_eigenvalue_separation","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MassGapFrontier.lean#L98-L105","doc":"**The crossing eigenvalue separation is `[2]_q`.**  The distance\nbetween the symmetric and antisymmetric channel eigenvalues is\n`q − (−q⁻¹) = q + q⁻¹ = [2]_q` — the quantum integer that\nnormalises the Markov trace (`tr_M = V/[2]_q^{c−1}`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.crossingEnergy_eq_eigenvalue_mean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.crossingEnergy_eq_eigenvalue_mean","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MassGapFrontier.lean#L83-L96","doc":"**The per-crossing energy is the mean of the two Hecke crossing\neigenvalues.**  The braiding eigenvalues on `S²V ⊕ Λ²V` are\n`q` (symmetric channel) and `−q⁻¹` (antisymmetric channel); their\nmean is exactly `E_×(q) = (q − q⁻¹)/2`.\n\nThis anchors the `CrossingFiltration` hypothesis in the\ncategorical source of `q`: the filtration asserts that every\nnon-vacuum excitation carries at least the *mean* spectral weight\nof one crossing. ","signatureChunk":0}]}